course: dictionary
lesson: 10551
title: Unauthorised means without permission
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at the parts of the word. Un- means not, and authorised means allowed by the person in charge. So unauthorised means done without permission. «Spending money from someone's card without permission is called an unauthorised payment; it is not okay, even in a family.» The words without permission are the clue.
explain: Signs use this word to keep people safe. «No unauthorised entry» means only people with permission may go in. «Unauthorised vehicles will be removed» means cars that are not allowed to park there will be taken away. Ask yourself: who is in charge here, and did they say yes?
explain: At school, an unauthorised absence means a day missed without a reason the school accepts. Online, using an account or computer without permission is unauthorised use, and it can be against the law. In every case, the word tells you that permission was missing.
fact: Unauthorised means done or used without permission from the person or group in charge.
fact: An unauthorised person is someone who is not allowed to be somewhere or to do something.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so unauthorised means not authorised.
fact: Phrases to know: unauthorised access, unauthorised absence, unauthorised use.
fact: Using an account or computer without permission can be against the law.
exercise: «Unauthorised vehicles will be removed.» What does unauthorised mean here? | Very fast | Painted in bright colours | Brand new | *Not allowed, so parked without permission
exercise: What does the sign «No unauthorised entry» tell you? | The door is painted blue | Everyone may go in for free | *Only people with permission may go in | Visitors must wear a hat
exercise: Which phrase means missing school without a reason the school accepts? | Sunny morning | *Unauthorised absence | Happy birthday | Hot dinner
test: «Spending money from someone's card without permission is called an unauthorised payment.» What is an unauthorised payment? | *Money spent without permission | A payment the family agreed to | A lost coin | Money given as a present
test: Using a friend's computer account without asking is what kind of use? | Authorised | *Unauthorised | Friendly | Shared
exam: Ravi reads «Unauthorised access is forbidden» on a school computer. What should he understand? | It means the computer is broken | *He must not use the computer without permission | It means the computer is new | He can use it if he is tired
